Z||000004||starfighter007@msn.com||08-29-2001||01:49 PM||||you dont have to buy anything yet pick there brains for the info that you need then shop around you will only get ripped off if you let them rip you of Oh and I think compotive wheels have what you would be looking for or why dont you look at some Ferrari recycleing yards and see if they have used wheels that you are looking for  and get wheel adapters ??||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FST2M6||08-29-2001||02:13 PM||||what are you looking at? (what wheel manufacturer?) the guy behind the counter won't be able to help you.. since your dealing with a differnt body on the car you'll need a differnt offset to fill the wheel wheels to near Ferrari Factory spec. contact the Wheel maker and the Body kit maker or fellow kit owner.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstmeatsig.jpg">          <BR>www.engineered.net||||reg||1
Z||000006||MinnGreenGT||08-29-2001||02:19 PM||||I've seen a new wheel measurement tool that a shop might have (or know who would have it).  it is completely adjustable to fit any bolt pattern, and can be adjusted to represent different offsets- allowing you to determine exactly what size wheel you'll need.  Sorry I don't know what it is called... just check around.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg"> <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000007||rogergarrison||08-29-2001||03:05 PM||||you need to know bolt pattern 100mm, I dont think anything wider than 10" will fit suspension, most important is the offset front and rear (where you want the front lip to sit in fender, most all Ferraris tire comes out flush or slighly inside the fender edges) I have 8" front and rear, with 5 1/2 backside setting offset on front and 4 1/2" backside setting on rear. Bilstein struts (OEM replacements) I got mine thru Team III Wheels (510) 895-8152/ 895-8880 Their drilled to fit Fiero pattern with no adapters.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/wheels_2.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>          <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=11878523&p=52990885">  <p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 08-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||rogergarrison||08-29-2001||04:45 PM||||bump||||reg||1
Z||000009||rogergarrison||08-29-2001||09:09 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by starfighter007@msn.com:<BR>compotive wheels have what you would be looking for or why dont you look at some Ferrari recycleing yards and see if they have used wheels that you are looking for  and get wheel adapters ??[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Wheel adapters break, ive had 2 that snapped.<P>as far as I know there are no Ferrari yards and none keep Ferraris. They either get sold wrecked to persons who rebuild them or to dealers who use them for parts. If you know any send me addys please. Ive tried all over the country. I find lots of them wrecked or burned out in Ebay for sale as is.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||fsrowsell||08-29-2001||10:09 PM||||Adrift, John Goods from Richards Landing ON is selling his Ferrari Rims and tires for a good price... <P>Posted To Kitcar List by: "John Good" &lt;2749@sympatico.ca&gt;<P>I have a set of Ferrari replica wheels with a Fiero bolt pattern I no longer<BR>need.  They are 15x8 and 15x7 and have mounted 265/50/15s and 195/50/15 tires<BR>in excellent shape.  The rims are polished and have no scratches or marks.  I<BR>would like to get about $700 for the set.  Email for pictures.<P>John Good<BR>Richards Landing, ON<BR>||||reg||1
